    "history_en": "Residents of the new market street raised money for this temple in 1856 and finished it in 1859. It is small, about 46 ping (roughly 152 square metres), and has stayed on the same spot on Dihua Street ever since. The main god is the Xia-Hai City God. A City God's Wife was added in 1893, and a statue of the Old Man under the Moon, the matchmaker god, arrived in 1971 and is now the most visited. The temple became a city monument on 19 August 1985. A 1994-1998 restoration was dedicated on 16 May 1998.",
