    "years": "renamed 31 Oct 2009; trial opening 6 Mar 2010; still open",
    "history_en": "The top floors of the Yongle Market building were a district activity centre from February 1987. The space was rebuilt from March 2009 as part of a city plan to revive old Dadaocheng, renamed Dadaocheng Theatre on 31 October 2009, and began trial operation on 6 March 2010. The 9th floor holds a 506-seat theatre for Taiwanese opera, Peking opera, Nanguan, Beiguan and Hakka opera. The 8th floor has a small hall of about 100 seats for glove puppetry and storytelling, plus a corridor exhibition on three puppet traditions. It is run by the Taipei Arts Promotion Office.",
