    "years": "In service since the tower opened, 2004-12-31; 101st-floor outdoor deck opened 2019-06-14",
    "history_en": "Near the top of Taipei 101 hangs a 660-tonne steel ball that visitors can walk up to. It is a tuned mass damper: a pendulum that swings against the tower's own sway in typhoons and earthquakes. The ball is 5.5 metres across, built from 41 stacked steel plates each 125 mm thick, and hangs between the 92nd and 88th floors, where the indoor observatory lets people look straight at it. Sanrio designed five Damper Baby mascots for it. After the April 2024 Hualien earthquake, news outlets worldwide pointed to this ball as the reason the tower came through.",
